## Existing operational interfaces

`run-native-build.py` accepts `--output-dir` and these authenticated `path#SHA`
operands (plus optional `--root`):

- `--build-source-manifest`, `--native-source-manifest`
- `--freeze-receipt`, `--freeze-execution`, `--scope-amendment`, `--scope-execution`
- `--fixed-input-guards-source`
- `--prior-final-preservation`, `--prior-retirement`, `--prior-retirement-execution`
- `--prior-native-build`, `--rad-native-build`
- `--prior-configure-execution`, `--prior-compile-execution`
- `--restore-configure-execution`

It keeps the prior CMake toolchain, arithmetic/warning options, source-dir
arguments and all inherited dependencies; changes only the project include
to the reviewed consumer recipe; adds `SURFACE_CONSUMER_SOURCE_DIR`; changes
only the target list to `surface_consumer_helper`, keeping parallel1/verbose.
It writes the same existing before-preservation and two command-receipt
shapes, with consumer-specific schema and direct actual authority refs.

`derive-and-describe-native-build.py` accepts `--before-preservation path#SHA`,
`--prior-derivation-execution path#SHA`, `--output-dir` (optional `--root`).
It requires exactly five new target object outputs and exactly five fresh
compile command lines. New registration rows are selected by resolved
`CMakeFiles/surface_consumer_helper.dir` output containment AND the exact five
Source paths. This is essential: the preserved717 already includes original
Pgm/CLI sources under energyplusapi. Source-filename-only selection would
wrongly remove those two old rows. Removing only the five new target rows
must leave the original717 dictionaries in their original order, unchanged.
No prior core/API object compilation is allowed; the two intentional new
target objects from original Pgm/CLI source are explicitly distinguished.

The generic `derive_native_helper.py` and `native_pe.py` are unchanged. The
prior accepted derivation argv supplies its exact strip authentication and
PE mechanism; only actual new Original path/SHA and fresh output directory
are replaced. Both Original and derivative are retained, with all existing
strict runtime-section/directory comparisons. The adapter has no strip,
provider or PE bypass, and supplies no retirement intent.

`complete-native-build-metadata.py` accepts `--before-preservation path#SHA`,
`--output-dir` (optional `--root`). It rechecks the exact ledger, source
identities, all50 protected objects, core631/12 and12 Original absences.
It records actual `path/sha256/size_bytes` for both new binaries. The output
build schema is `ctf10-surface-consumer-native-build.v1`, target
`surface_consumer_helper`, status `pass-actual-5TU-link-and-preservation`.
`native_source_files` contains five TUs plus the header and recipe;
`compiled_source_files` contains only the five actual TUs.

## Actual link-provider obligation

Five target object LOAD records must precede `Products/libenergypluslib.a`.
Eight selected actual symbol definitions must each fall inside the latest
actual `.text` section's address range and have the exact target provider:
six HBSM entry/history/report/CTF-only functions from the reviewed full derived
HBSM, global `EnergyPlusPgm` from original Pgm, and `ProcessArgs` from original
CLI. Selection uses source-owned function names, not a guessed ABI signature.
Any selected original core HBSM object occurrence fails. Genuine core HBM and
Construction remain allowed and required by the unchanged normal engine;
old RAD/CTF no-provider predicates are not misapplied to this target.

The preservation output stores `address_bound_selected_providers` (actual
symbol and section lines), actual five target LOAD records,
`selected_core_HeatBalanceSurfaceManager_object_hits`, compile correspondence,
direct restoration/RAD/scope/freeze identities and the actual SourceSnapshot.
